    tll_reading="The archive reads the readers as an authored receiving apparatus whose reading emits writing, the σ : ⟨x, M₀⟩ → ⟨x, M₁, y⟩ of #1543 built by hand before the large models: the project states that its readers, 'composed by the words within which they move', also 'write', and How It Is in Common Tongues carries Beckett's text through a search engine's index and back as recomposition with each phrase sourced to a URL, a date and a count, a pre-LLM case of reading-to-composition with phrase-level provenance kept, near the search-layer lineage #186 assigns to Flarf. It is electronic literature with an index and a search engine as its apparatus; the saved sources make no claim about model training.",
    data_access="the readers' outputs published on the web as live streams; How It Is in Common Tongues downloadable as a pdf and obtainable as a print copy against a donation",
    license="not stated in the saved sources; How It Is in Common Tongues is 'officially hors de commerce', with surplus over costs donated to the EFF and related groups",
